{#intro .lead}
# Getting started

The *garden planner* helps you decide _what_ to plant and _when_. It is
written in Rust, configured with KDL and documented in Djot -- a light
markup language that's "easier" to parse than Markdown... mostly.

Use `cargo run --release` to build it, press [Ctrl+C]{.kbd} to stop, and
read the [installation guide][install] or <https://example.com/docs> for
details. Questions go to <help@example.com>.

## Text formatting

Djot has {=highlighted=}, {+inserted+} and {-deleted-} text, H~2~O and
E = mc^2^, plus *strong*, _emphasis_ and *_both at once_*. A span can carry
[attributes]{#note-1 .warning key="value"} and so can `code`{.rust}.

Inline math works too: $`\sum_{i=1}^n i = \frac{n(n+1)}{2}`, and raw HTML
can be passed through with `<kbd>Esc</kbd>`{=html}.

Symbols like :sunflower: and :tomato: become emoji, a backslash escapes
\*literal asterisks\*, and a trailing backslash forces a line break\
right here. Write x{^2^} or x{~i~}, use 'single quotes', and
an em dash---like this. See [the guide][] or [the FAQ](faq.dj), and
![a logo][logo] or ![a badge][]. Comments {% like this %} can also sit inline.

![Raised beds in spring](beds.jpg){width=600}

See the footnote for history.[^history]

## Lists

1. Choose a site with at least six hours of sun.
2. Test the soil:
   - pH between 6.0 and 7.0
   - good drainage
3. Plan your beds.

- [ ] order seeds
- [x] build compost bin

